commit c7c344e2fc7954885732b0e6ea81579f6485ddf6
Author: Liz <liz@gewelf.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 22:39:24 2026 -0400

    hardening: format parsers free partial allocations on OOM; duplicate footer lists

    Statistics, GeospatialStatistics, ColumnMetaData, ColumnChunk, RowGroup,
    KeyValue and SchemaElement now have deinit() and an errdefer in parse(),
    so a failing parse frees what it had allocated. FileMetaData's free
    helpers moved onto those deinit methods.

    A repeated Thrift field used to overwrite the earlier value and leak it.
    Repeated footer lists (schema, row_groups, key_value_metadata) and the
    other owned fields now free the earlier value before replacing it.

    Tests: a FailingAllocator sweep over FileMetaData.parse of
    basic_types_plain_uncompressed (fail_index 0..63 all fail cleanly, 64
    succeeds) and a hand-built footer with a repeated schema list.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M67X6ZRWWQPZX0EZWQG1F6YN

